{{fbdoc item="title" value="SDL, the Simple DirectMedia Layer"}}----
Cross-platform multimedia library and rendering API.

This repository contains bindings for three SDL API generations. Their C
interfaces reuse many names, so use one generation per source module.

Website: http://www.libsdl.org
Platforms supported: Win32, Linux, FreeBSD (selected examples), Haiku (SDL 1.2)

Core headers and examples:

* SDL 1.2.15: inc/SDL/SDL.bi and examples/graphics/SDL1/
* SDL 2.0.14: inc/SDL2/SDL.bi and examples/graphics/SDL2/
* SDL 3.4.18: inc/SDL3/SDL.bi and examples/graphics/SDL3/

Companion bindings and examples:

* SDL 1.2: SDL_image, SDL_gfx, SDL_mixer, SDL_net, SDL_Pango, SDL_rtf,
  SDL_sound, SDL_ttf, SDL_gpu, and SDL_FontCache.
* SDL 2: SDL2_image, SDL2_gfx, SDL2_mixer, SDL2_net, SDL2_rtf,
  SDL2_sound, SDL2_ttf, SDL2_gpu, SDL2_bgi, and SDL2_FontCache.
* SDL 3: SDL3_image, SDL3_mixer, SDL3_net, SDL3_sound, and SDL3_ttf.
  The core binding also covers GPU, Vulkan, SDL_test, and the TTF text engine.
  Additional bindings and examples cover SDL3_gfx, SDL3_bgi, SDL3_rtf, and
  SDL3_shadercross.

The pinned SDL 3 companion releases are SDL3_image 3.4.8, SDL3_mixer 3.2.4,
SDL3_net 3.2.0, SDL3_sound 3.2.0, and SDL3_ttf 3.2.2. SDL3_sound decodes
audio files; SDL3_mixer provides mixing and playback tracks.

Haiku R1 beta 6 amd64: examples/graphics/SDL1/core/video_info.bas compiled and
ran with FreeBASIC 1.20.4-3 against HaikuPorts SDL 1.2.15. This headless check
covered SDL initialization and video-info queries; it did not open a window or
test rendering. SDL 2 and SDL 3 remain unqualified on Haiku.

FreeBSD runtime checks passed for the SDL 1.2 video-info example under Xvfb
and for SDL 3 core, image, TrueType, and network examples under Xvfb or the
local resolver. The SDL 1.2 driver name was blank in the headless run.
SDL 2 runtime examples did not complete in the qualification harness. Runtime
support for the other companion examples, audio devices, and physical displays
has not been established. Several optional libraries also lacked matching
linkable packages in the checked FreeBSD package set; see
doc/freebsd-example-qualification.md for the exact scope.

